# Common laptop/desktop runtime additions. RavenGUI itself ships in the image.
linux-firmware
sof-firmware
alsa-ucm-conf
pipewire
pipewire-audio
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
bluez
bluez-utils
mesa-utils
vulkan-tools
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel

# The graphics stack huginn links against.
#
# The ISO stages these as bare .so files copied off the build host -- stage2's
# copy_libraries() and stage-gui.sh's stage_gui_libraries(). That is what makes
# the live image work, but `rvn owns` reports no package owns any of them, so
# on an installed system they were invisible to the package manager: never
# updated, never repaired, and no way to tell a corrupted one from a missing
# one. Declaring them here puts the same files under package management on any
# machine that asked for a desktop.
#
# These are the runtime half of ravengui's [dependencies] in
# packages/gui/ravengui/package.toml; keep the two in step.
#
# Two names from that list are deliberately absent. `libseat` is not a package
# on Arch -- the library ships inside seatd, so seatd covers both the daemon
# and the .so huginn links. `libudev` is not a package either; it comes from
# systemd-libs, which is already a base dependency. Listing either by name
# fails the whole profile, because raven-postinstall hands the entire list to
# one `rvn install`.
mesa
libdrm
libinput
libxkbcommon
wayland
seatd
xorg-xwayland

# The toolkit, for RavenFileManager.
#
# The image ships it -- stage-gui.sh builds it from javanhut/RavenFileManager
# alongside huginn and the terminal -- and, like the graphics stack above, it
# arrives as unowned files copied off a build host. It links a hundred and
# thirty-four shared libraries against huginn's seventeen, so the great
# majority of these come in as dependencies of gtk4 and libadwaita; they are
# named anyway, because a package that is installed as a dependency is one an
# unrelated removal can take with it.
#
# Four are here for reasons no linker reports:
#
#   glib2                      owns glib-compile-schemas. GSettings reads only
#                              the compiled gschemas.compiled, never the XML,
#                              and without it every GTK application aborts at
#                              startup on a schema lookup.
#   gsettings-desktop-schemas  libadwaita reads org.gnome.desktop.interface to
#                              choose light or dark; absent, it stays light.
#   shared-mime-info           without mime.cache every file reads as
#                              application/octet-stream.
#   bubblewrap                 since gdk-pixbuf 2.44 the image loaders live in
#                              glycin, which decodes inside a bwrap sandbox and
#                              refuses to decode without one. No bwrap, no
#                              images anywhere in the toolkit.
#
# Installing these is necessary and not sufficient: the caches above are
# derived state and nothing here rebuilds them. `raven-desktopinstall` is the
# script that installs this set *and* rebuilds them, and is the better command
# to reach for on an already-installed machine.
gtk4
libadwaita
glib2
gsettings-desktop-schemas
gsettings-system-schemas
shared-mime-info
desktop-file-utils
gtk-update-icon-cache
gdk-pixbuf2
librsvg
glycin
bubblewrap
dconf
